title: A read-only file says it could not be saved and stays unsaved; Save and close writes the others and keeps the app open instead of losing the text
folders: edit-readonly
limit: 50
allow-log: cannot save
forbid-log: cannot edit
forbid-log: nothing offers
expect-log: cannot save .*locked\.txt
expect-log: script: Answer\("Close without saving"\)
expect-file: edit-readonly/locked.txt :: (?-i)\Alocked one\nlocked two\n\z
expect-file: edit-readonly/free.txt :: (?-i)\AFfree one\nfree two\n\z

wait 3000
goto locked.txt
wait 800
edit locked.txt 1 1
type L
key save
wait 800
mark save-failed
wait 400
edit free.txt 1 1
type F
quit
wait 1000
answer Save and close
wait 1200
mark still-open
wait 400
quit
wait 1000
mark asked-again
wait 400
answer Close without saving
wait 800
